What is Kubernetes Architecture?

Kubernetes architecture is built on a highly resilient Master–Worker design that allows us to run applications at massive scale with automation, reliability, and self-healing capabilities.

🔹 Control Plane – Where We Make Decisions
We rely on the control plane to manage the entire cluster.
 It includes:
API Server – the central access point for everything in the cluster
etcd – the source of truth where cluster state is stored
Scheduler – intelligently picks the best node for each Pod
Controller Manager – constantly monitors and corrects cluster state
These components work together so we always maintain the desired state.

🔹 Worker Nodes – Where We Run Our Applications
Our workloads run on worker nodes, each powered by:
kubelet – ensures containers are healthy and running
kube-proxy – manages all networking and service routing
Container Runtime – executes containers efficiently
This layer ensures our applications are always available, scalable, and stable.
